LICENCE

1. This project's own work: no rights claimed
---------------------------------------------

The following are dedicated to the public domain under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal
Public Domain Dedication (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/):

- the code (HTML, CSS, JavaScript and Python);
- the hand transcriptions of the census tables;
- the checks, crosswalks, alias tables and documentation;
- the text of the site.

To the extent possible under law, all copyright and related or neighbouring rights in them are
waived. They may be copied, modified and used for any purpose without permission or attribution.

This waiver does not cover the third-party material listed in section 2. That material stays under
its own terms, and so does any file derived from it.


2. Third-party data and its licences
------------------------------------

Census of India, 1931 (the figures and the page scans)
  Government of India publications, 1932-1934: public domain.
  The scans used are on the Internet Archive; item identifiers are listed in README.md and docs/regional.md.

plague_india, 1931 province boundaries (W. Tennant), https://github.com/wtennant/plague_india
  GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0 (LGPL-3.0). The licence text is in source/geo/plague_india/LICENSE.
  Applies to: source/geo/plague_india/*, and the 1931 unit geometry derived from it in data/geo.js
  and data/units1931.geojson.

geoBoundaries (William & Mary geoLab), https://www.geoboundaries.org/
  India ADM1/ADM2: Open Database License 1.0 (ODbL).
  Pakistan ADM2: public domain.
  Bangladesh ADM2: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 IGO (CC BY 3.0 IGO).
  Citation: Runfola, D. et al. (2020) geoBoundaries: A global database of political administrative
  boundaries. PLoS ONE 15(4): e0231866.
  Applies to: data/geo.js (boundary refinement), data/units1931.geojson, and data/districts.js
  (present-day district geometry). The geometry in these files that derives from geoBoundaries India
  is made available under the ODbL 1.0.

OpenStreetMap, outline of the Rann of Kutch
  (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License 1.0 (ODbL), https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  Applies to: source/geo/rann_of_kutch_osm.geojson, and the Rann outline in data/geo.js.

Natural Earth, https://www.naturalearthdata.com/
  Public domain.
  Applies to: coastlines, neighbouring countries and graticule in data/geo.js, and the Myanmar
  states/regions in data/districts.js.

Burma 1931 districts and states: administrative layer of the Japanese Empire map
  https://froginawell.net/reference/japanese-empire/ (japan-empire-map-admin.svg), used with permission.
  Applies to: source/geo/burma_1931_districts.geojson and the Burma units in data/districts.js.

India State and District Evolution Database, 1872-2025 (ISDED)
  Jolad, Shivakumar; Kalra, Ayushi; Singh, Mahendra. Harvard Dataverse, doi:10.7910/DVN/D1AGUR.
  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
  Applies to: the district lineage used to group units in data/districts.js, data/regional_table15.csv
  and docs/regional_area_crosswalk.csv. The database itself is not redistributed here.

Census of India 2011, Table A-2 (decadal variation in population since 1901), district level
  Office of the Registrar General and Census Commissioner, India. Government of India published data.
  Applies to: the 1901-2011 population series in data/districts.js. The spreadsheet itself is not
  redistributed here.

Source Serif 4 (Adobe), loaded from Google Fonts at page view
  SIL Open Font License 1.1. Not redistributed here.
